A||||12||2M4 Dale||Power trunk switch ?||||5||
Z||000000||2M4 Dale||05-20-2000||08:26 PM||||It seems as though I have the trunk lock release soleniod and the wires on my trunk catch. Is all I need to do is mount/plug in  a switch on the dash to get this thing working ? My EconoCoupe don't have the switch.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||05-21-2000||12:45 AM||||The factory routed the circuit through the emergency brake light switch so the trunk won't activate with the Fiero running without you pull the brake lever.  Perhaps this is to prevent objects floating around the cockpit at speed from impacting the switch and causing the Fiero to launch into the air and burst into flames?<P>Your call.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-21-2000||02:58 PM||||Likely someone replaced the lid and that was on it. You still need the rest of the materials in the trunk lid install article. <P>Manual tranny cars interlock thru the hand brake. Automatics interlock tru the neutral start switch.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||05-22-2000||12:25 AM||||I may be wrong but I think all cars have the wiring. All the ones I have seen do. Since you have a deck lid with the goods you will need to get the relay that plugs in under the dash and the switch. Pull the bezel on the right of the dash and see if the plug is there. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||05-22-2000||08:29 AM||||I posted a question about this same thing last friday. Do a search for it or go to orge's cave link on the bottom of the page for real good info. And yes all cars came pre-wired for the trunk release and re-defroster set-up.||||reg||14
Z||000005||2M4 Dale||05-23-2000||06:56 AM||||Thanks Guys. I'll have a power trunk release soon.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Carrolles||05-23-2000||12:58 PM||||On my 85SE v-6 4spd I can open the trunk release at any time whether the ignition is on or off, engine running or not, in gear or not, parking brake on or off.  It does not appear to have been tampered with either.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||05-23-2000||02:48 PM||||a little off topic, but noticed someone mentioned rear defroster. Has anyone ever had to use it? on mine, the engine heat makes the glass almost hot enough to cook on, personally i think its totally useless. I drive year round and NEVER have turned it on, finally took out the switch and used the space to mount my driving lite switch.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||05-23-2000||03:20 PM||||I use mine. ||||reg||1
