Z||000012||Carrolles||05-24-2000||12:52 PM||||When I have to park outside during the winter I turn on the rear defogger as soon as I crank the engine.  By the time I get buckled up and get everything situated I can see out the rear glass to back out of the driveway.  I then turn it off because the engine does give off enough heat to keep it clear.||||reg||1
